  "line": "Sodom was a wicked city on the well-watered plain of the Jordan, where Lot made his home and which God destroyed with sulfur and fire.",
  "moments": [
    {
      "title": "Lot Settles Near Sodom",
      "text": "Lot looked over the well-watered plain and chose it for himself. He pitched his tent toward Sodom, though its men were wicked and sinned greatly against the LORD.",
      "passage": "Genesis 13:9-13"
    },
    {
      "title": "Lot Is Carried Off",
      "text": "Four kings seized the goods of Sodom and Gomorrah. They also carried off Lot and his possessions, since he was living in Sodom.",
      "passage": "Genesis 14:10-12"
    },
    {
      "title": "Angels Visit Lot",
      "text": "Two angels came to Sodom, and Lot welcomed them into his house. That night the men of the city surrounded the house, and the angels struck them with blindness.",
      "passage": "Genesis 19:1-12"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sodom Destroyed",
      "text": "The LORD rained sulfur and fire on Sodom and Gomorrah from the heavens. Abraham saw smoke rising like smoke from a furnace, and God remembered him and brought Lot out.",
      "passage": "Genesis 19:23-29"
    }
  ],
